\sum_{k=0}^{n} \\binom{n}{k} = 2^n\n\\]\nThe arithmetic mean of the elements in the \\( n \\)-th row is the sum of the elements divided by the number of elements. Therefore, the arithmetic mean \\( M \\) of the elements in the \\( n \\)-th row is:\n\\[\nM = \\frac{2^n}{n+1}\n\\]\nWe are given that the arithmetic mean is 51.2. So we set up the equation:\n\\[\n\\frac{2^n}{n+1} = 51.2\n\\]\nTo find \\( n \\), we need to solve this equation. First, we can try to find an approximate value of \\( n \\) by testing some values.\n\nIf \\( n = 9 \\):\n\\[\n\\frac{2^9}{9+1} = \\frac{512}{10} = 51.2\n\\]\nThis satisfies the equation. Therefore, the value of \\( n \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{9}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{9}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
